    {
      "text": "Knots and the Maxwell Equations — In this chapter, we review the Ra˜nada ﬁeld line solutions of Maxwell’s equations in the vacuum, which describe a topologically non-trivial electro- magnetic ﬁeld\n\n**Knots and the Maxwell Equations**\n\n*Ion V. Vancea*\n\n26 pp, 10 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this chapter, we review the Ra˜nada ﬁeld line solutions of Maxwell’s equations in the vacuum, which describe a topologically non-trivial electro- magnetic ﬁeld, as well as their relation with the knot theory. Also, we present a generalization of these solutions to the non-linear electrodynamics recently published in the literature.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Maxwell's equations; 2.1 Maxwell's equations in the three-dimension; 2.2 Maxwell equations in covariant formulation; 3 Knots in Maxwell's electrodynamics; 3.1 Ranãda solutions; 3.2 Electromagnetic knot fields; 4 Electric and magnetic knots in Bateman param; 5 Knots in nonlinear electrodynamics",
      "lang": "en",
      "state": "draft",
